# Prettier owns the JavaScript and Vue sources; everything else keeps its current
# shape. Prettier 3 also reads .gitignore by default, so build output stays out.

# Markdown / Cursor rules — no Prettier (Cursor renders MD natively; preserve source as-is)
*.md
*.mdc

# Styles feed the LESS/CSS build, markup is imported verbatim by the bundles, and the
# data/config files are either generated (CLDR, language packs, metrics) or hand-tuned
# around external contracts (workflow job names, Prettier's own options).
*.less
*.css
*.html
*.json
*.yml
*.yaml
.prettierrc

# Compiled, bundled and vendored sources — same set the ESLint config ignores.
**/assets/
**/bundle/
**/vendor/
node_modules/
packages/composer/
storage/
tmp/
*.min.js
